\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The initial Topic~5 Jacobian spectrum scaled by $h=0.05$ and $h=0.10$. The two categorical rows distinguish step sizes; their vertical positions do not represent imaginary parts. The $+0.88$ mode reflects physical growth of the initially small singular value, while $h=0.10$ moves the fastest negative mode past Euler's $-2$ boundary.}}{14}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
